= Dire Economics

After the construction bubble popped and the 2008 global economic crash, many countries in the Eurozone are struggling to recover. With the European Central Bank having had to already intervene in Greece, Ireland, Portugal, and now Spain, the public debt situation is only aggravating the situation. Catalonia, traditionally one of the few industrialized regions of Spain is, nonetheless, no exception. Structurally infra-financed and with poor debt standings, it seems like working people are once again the ones suffering the most, thanks in no minor part to the austerity budgets approved by a CiU - PPC alliance.

